{
  "an3.73:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 3.73 ",
  "an3.73:0.2": "8. Ānanda ",
  "an3.73:0.3": "With Mahānāma the Sakyan ",
  "an3.73:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "an3.73:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying in the land of the Sakyans, near Kapilavatthu in the Banyan Tree Monastery. ",
  "an3.73:1.3": "Now at that time the Buddha had recently recovered from an illness. ",
  "an3.73:1.4": "Then Mahānāma the Sakyan went up to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him: ",
  "an3.73:1.5": "“For a long time, sir, I have understood your teaching like this: ",
  "an3.73:1.6": "‘Knowledge is for those with immersion, not those without immersion.’ ",
  "an3.73:1.7": "But, sir, does immersion come first, then knowledge? ",
  "an3.73:1.8": "Or does knowledge come first, then immersion?” ",
  "an3.73:1.9": "Then Venerable Ānanda thought, ",
  "an3.73:1.10": "“The Buddha has recently recovered from an illness, ",
  "an3.73:1.11": "and this Mahānāma asks him a question that’s too deep. ",
  "an3.73:1.12": "Why don’t I take him off to one side and teach him the Dhamma?” ",
  "an3.73:2.1": "Then Ānanda took Mahānāma by the arm, led him off to one side, and said to him, ",
  "an3.73:2.2": "“Mahānāma, the Buddha has spoken of the ethics, immersion, and wisdom of a trainee; and the ethics, immersion, and wisdom of an adept. ",
  "an3.73:2.3": "What is the ethics of a trainee? ",
  "an3.73:2.4": "It’s when a mendicant is ethical, restrained in the monastic code, conducting themsel